.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-harness-golden - Take the nested harness's golden point (690-692)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge harness golden <target-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Take a disk-only golden snapshot (pvh-golden) of the nested harness VMs
690, 691 and 692 after a graceful shutdown, then start them and accept the
nested cluster. Never destroys a VM. With --replace-golden every existing
golden is deleted first. The storage is checked by the capability probe's
static layer; the three VMs are locked for the whole run.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for golden

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="kv"
	output format: "kv" or "json"

.PP
\fB--pool\fP="pveforge-harness"
	harness pool a VM must be a member of

.PP
\fB--replace-golden\fP[=false]
	delete any existing golden first (never a mix of old and new)

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)

.PP
\fB--storage\fP=""
	the outer storage id (or $HARNESS_STORAGE)

.PP
\fB--tag\fP="pveforge-harness"
	harness tag a VM must carry


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-harness(1)\fP
